  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>l</mi></math> be the length of the cylinder in water it is in the vertical position and <math><mi>A</mi></math> be the cross-sectional area of the cylinder. As cylinder is floating so<br/><br/>Weight of cylinder = upward thrust<math><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi> </mi><mi>l</mi><mi> </mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> or <math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>ρ</mi></math><br/><br/>When the cylinder is tilled through an angle <math><mi>θ</mi></math>, length of cylinder in water <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></math><br/><br/>Weight of water displaced <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi> </mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br/><br/>Restoring force <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>l</mi><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi><mi> </mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi><mi> </mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br/><br/><math><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi><mi> </mi><mi>ρ</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi ma